                "firstName": "A.",
                "lastName": "Birrell"
            }
        ],
        "abstract": "The Apollo project with its complex global communication satellite support network represents the most significant programme yet planned in space exploration, and bearing in mind that it will be only ten years in October this year since Russia launched the first satellite, it serves to highlight the tremendous achievements in science and technology of the past decade. It is pleasing to communications engineers that the paper presented this evening deals with the provision of global communications via earth satellites, which will be one of the greatest benefits to all nations that has emerged as a result of the space research programmes. Further, the emphasis is on the design requirements of earth stations for operation in conjunction with earth satellites, a subject which is becoming of increasing interest to many Administrations not yet committed to the establishment of earth stations.",
